# s3-15 core wire (GNOME Shell extension kept installed while Computer Use is on)

## mixdog-tools: native/core/crates/mixdog-tools/src/desktop/mod.rs
After `mod computer_gnome;` add:
    pub mod computer_gnome_extension;
(`pub`, because the daemon's config handler calls it; if desktop/mod.rs re-exports a facade instead, re-export
`computer_gnome_extension::{apply_gnome_extension, bundled_dir, GnomeExtensionState}` there.)

## Dependencies
None: it uses async-trait, serde, serde_json, tokio, tokio-util, tracing and mixdog-core-api, all already [dependencies] of mixdog-tools.

## The one call (compose_flip.rs `compose_real`, Linux only, a no-op elsewhere)
Right after `late_computer_hosts.bind(computer_pool.clone())...?;` (the place Computer Use is composed), add:
    {
        // GNOME window control comes from Mixdog's own shell extension: keep it installed and enabled exactly while Computer Use
        // is on (port of the desktop's applyGnomeExtensionSetting; a no-op off GNOME).
        let (config, manager, cancel) = (config.clone(), b.process_manager.clone(), b.cancel.clone());
        let mut changes = config.changes();
        tokio::spawn(async move {
            use mixdog_tools::desktop::computer_gnome_extension::{apply_gnome_extension, bundled_dir};
            let exe_dir = std::env::current_exe().ok().and_then(|exe| exe.parent().map(std::path::Path::to_path_buf)).unwrap_or_default();
            loop {
                let enabled = config.desktop_settings().computer_control;
                let env: mixdog_tools::desktop::computer_linux::Env = std::env::vars().collect();
                apply_gnome_extension(manager.clone(), enabled, &env, bundled_dir(&env, &exe_dir).as_deref(), &cancel).await;
                if !matches!(cancel.run_until_cancelled(changes.changed()).await, Some(Ok(()))) {
                    break;
                }
            }
        });
    }
(At start it applies the current value, then again after every config change, as the desktop re-applied it on every settings
apply (each step is idempotent, and an extension toggled by hand is brought back in line); the env is the process env, as the Linux preflight reads it
(`LinuxSession::of_host`). The bundle is optional: without one, off still takes the uuid out of the enabled list.)
`diagnose` already reports the result: computer_gnome::linux_permissions adds `gnome_extension` {installed, enabled, needsRelogin, error?}.

## Packaging (the packaging task of the wave, not s3-15)
The extension payload native/gnome-extension/mixdog-windows@mixdog.io must be found by bundled_dir: next to the executable in
`gnome-extension/mixdog-windows@mixdog.io`, or `resources/gnome-extension/...` beside it (electron-builder.yml already copies it to
resources/gnome-extension/ for the desktop app); MIXDOG_GNOME_EXTENSION_DIR overrides. The .deb ships it system-wide already.

## SERVICE_PENDING
Nothing to remove: no protocol method is added.

## Desktop (after wiring, s3-26)
apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts applyComputerControlSetting: drop the applyGnomeExtensionSetting call and its import;
delete apps/desktop/src/main/computer/host/gnome-extension.ts and gnome-extension.test.mjs.
